WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.100
Escape From Side One

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:50.050
We've lost half of our mobile suits.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.890
You're Titans only by name.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:52.920
Lieutenant Commander...!

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:55.350
Lila's troops are doing better than ours.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.720
Well, actually...!

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.320
Defending Jerid?

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.630
No, it's just that I'd like you to understand
that the enemy was especially skilled.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:04.630
I don't understand.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.190
I'm not too familiar with the White Base
when it was active, but the Argama...

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:10.860
...seemed to be like the White Base.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.370
What gives you that feeling?

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.770
At first it looks wide open to attack,
but you soon find out it's well guarded.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.980
In particular, the Gundam Mk. IIs
look amateurish at first glance...

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:25.020
...but when actually fighting against them,
their retaliatory power is incredible.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.630
<i>Lieutenant Commander.</i>

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.890
<i>The enemy fleet appears to be</i>
<i>headed directly to the Side 4 district.</i>

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.300
What?!

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.560
Is it entering the debris cluster
to try to shake us off?

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.000
They could be Newtypes.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.040
Don't be silly! There is no such thing!

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:47.080
Newtypes are imaginary beings
created by media hype!

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.850
You're making me an official pilot?

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.720
Naturally, after seeing your heroics
out there.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.420
I darted off on my own...

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.250
...so I thought I'd be
thrown in a cell for my actions.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.580
You didn't mean it, did you?

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:11.970
Presently on the Argama, we have
the GM pilots from the Mont Blanc...

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.270
...so we don't need your help right away.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.670
However, I'd like to see how much
further we can develop your skills.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.470
So, I'm an experiment for Newtypes.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.100
We can leave that
to other research laboratories.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:26.850
I'm more concerned about
your role as part of this ship.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.620
After all, the Argama's a military ship.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.620
A soldier? At my age?

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:38.660
In the previous great war, the White Base had
many crew members your age.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:43.700
Besides, there is a drastic shortage
of elder soldiers within the Earth sphere.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:45.800
I'm aware of that.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.710
I'd like some time to think this over.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.000
I'm of the same opinion
as Commodore Blex.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.210
I'm very interested in your abilities.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:59.310
Is it right to send a youngster out to war,
just because you're interested?

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.640
You're being very critical.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.320
There's no way of finding
Amuro Ray's whereabouts...

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.650
...by searching the personnel records.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:10.830
Can't you find the Newtype who piloted
the previous Gundam?

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:11.660
That's right.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.670
That's the kind of military
the Earth Federation Forces is now.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:20.070
The souls of the people living on Earth
are attracted by its gravity, so they can't fly.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.330
So how's my becoming a pilot
going to change anything?

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.270
For one, the souls of Earth's people...!

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:29.640
- That has nothing to do with me, does it?!
- Do you think so?

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.840
Will the Argama treat me
with equal benefits of a Lieutenant?

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:35.820
That's possible.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.360
Why did you become a soldier, Lieutenant?

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.550
Why a soldier?

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.460
I'd like to know.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.020
Because it's the only way I know how
to make a living.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.630
That's why I never got married.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.610
The ship has entered the Side 4 district!

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.580
<i>We're locking down the residential district.</i>

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.410
<i>All crew, change into normal suits.</i>

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:03.710
<i>Be on alert!</i>

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.800
<i>I know you're in there!</i>

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:28.570
<i>Open up, Lieutenant!</i>

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.140
What do you want?!

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:33.970
You shouldn't need me for anything!

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.480
Why'd you stand up for me
in front of Jamaican?!

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:43.820
Sorry.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.780
What's this about Jamaican?

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.830
I told you I want to lead the Titans someday,
didn't I?

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:54.000
To do that, I want to deal with guys
like Jamaican alone!

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.700
Standing up for me like that...!

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.870
Doesn't sound like you at all,
the person who lectured me!

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:04.130
I don't think you were listening
to what I was saying.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.280
I was talking to him about the Argama.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.750
I wasn't thinking about you one bit.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:15.710
- I had already heard about Newtypes!
- Don't you dare look this way!

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:20.450
Commander, it appears that Gryps
has begun its move at last.

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:22.490
I see. Finally.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:26.130
- And the enemy spaceship?
- It's entered the debris cluster.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:31.630
It's either headed for Side 2 or the Moon.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.870
A mid-sized drifting object
detected ahead of us to the starboard!

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:40.910
Move bow slightly!

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.220
Above left! A small rock!

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.190
Lieutenant Emma has excellent eyesight.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:58.660
This is the third one!

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:01.290
She isn't a Titan officer for nothing.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.660
<i>Former,</i> that is.
Please don't overlook that fact.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:08.470
At this rate, there's no way of determining
whether the Argama...

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:11.340
...is going to Side 1, the Moon, or Side 2!

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.350
That's why we should split our fleet
into three...!

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:16.510
Lieutenant!

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.780
I'm the strategic advisor!

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:23.220
We must repay the Alexandria...

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.480
...for the repairs they did
to the Galbaldy mobile suits.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.920
We are not Titans,
so we will return to the Bosnia...

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:32.190
...pursue the Argama using a different
route, and stop them there.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.130
Good idea...

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.690
...but refrain from rushing into a battle
when you catch up to the enemy.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:40.340
I heard that you're the type
who loves war, Lieutenant.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:42.770
That's just your biased opinion,
Lieutenant Commander!

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:44.580
Very well.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:48.210
I'll leave you in charge of what to do
if you contact the enemy...

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.310
...but your main objective
shall be to meet up with us.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:52.680
Yes, sir! Let's go!

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:56.150
- We're moving!
- Yes, ma'am.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.320
Lieutenant Lila, you know now, right?

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.860
I already knew what Jamaican would say.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:03.900
Then why did you...?

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:07.620
I wanted to make it clear to you
how I dislike those types of men!

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:10.900
Lila!

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:14.130
How about getting together for a drink
sometime?

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:17.200
- I'll think about it.
- Thank you.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:21.800
If you become a fine man,
I can lean on you and drink.

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.850
It'll be nice.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:39.320
You have what it takes
to become a fine man.

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:47.370
<i>Observers, come aboard! Observers!</i>

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:49.400
Come aboard!

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:51.440
- Lieutenant Quattro!
- <i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.740
- Oh, where's Lieutenant Emma?
- <i>For what, sir?</i>

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:56.510
Well, uh... I need a talk with her.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.720
<i>Understood, sir.</i>
<i>I'll send her up to the bridge later.</i>

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:11.620
Not yet?! Haven't you found it yet?!

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:13.450
Don't be so impatient.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.290
I guess they aren't heading for Side 1.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:19.970
I found them!

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.840
- Are you sure?!
- It's the Argama!

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.470
The radar is showing a ship
with an identical shape. I'm sure of it.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:27.040
We guessed right.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:29.550
Lila, do we stand a chance?

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.810
It's hard to tell at this point,
but I'll make it for sure.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:35.380
We'll make it clear that the Titans
aren't the only force around.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:37.750
Thank you very much, Captain.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.060
Well, you see... actually...!

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.530
<i>Approaching Colony 30!</i>

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.530
This is the colony that I'd like you to see.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:52.840
It explains why we started our movement
against the Earth Federation Government.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:53.870
Yes, sir.

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.680
The Argama appears to have docked
at Colony 30.

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:39.780
Colony 30?! That place is where...

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:43.290
It's where the citizens were wiped out
because of the operation.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.550
Why should the A.E.U.G.
want to visit here?

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.950
Could this be the A.E.U.G.'s secret hideout?

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:51.720
It could very well be the perfect hideout,
because of its present state.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:56.370
I'll check it out. Take a detour and let me
enter from the industrial hatch...

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:58.270
...so that I can enter
unnoticed by the enemy.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:02.170
Shouldn't you wait
for the Alexandria to arrive first?

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:06.570
Wouldn't it be better if we could advise
Lt. Commander Jamaican of the situation?

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:09.040
Well, that's true.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:11.080
I'm only going to check things out.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.750
Return as soon as you've determined
whether or not there's a base there, all right?!

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:44.180
- What's that?
- A mummy. A human mummy.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:45.680
Mummies?

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.180
Because the mirror in the colony
no longer moves.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:17.150
Why are the corpses left like this?!

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:19.240
There are too many to bury.

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:21.510
How can anyone kill people like this?!

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:26.160
Because they're not killing with their
own hands.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:30.330
If their hands aren't soiled with blood,
they don't realize the pain inflicted.

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:37.400
I guess not.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.240
So, these are the tanks of poisonous gas.

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:08.200
There's electricity.
Is the A.E.U.G. using this colony?

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.150
Is he a member of the A.E.U.G.?!

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:28.550
This colony remains dead.

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:33.890
Which means it'll be the perfect colony
for the A.E.U.G. to use as a secret base.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:36.590
Yes. Shall we make our way to the spaceport?

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:41.760
Looks like we can use this.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:47.000
Seemingly they didn't even have the time
to think of their own deaths.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:51.440
Lieutenant, you may feel that
the A.E.U.G....

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:54.410
...was at fault for staging
a demonstration here.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:14:00.710
But consider this. If the people on Earth
think only about reconstructing Earth...

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:04.480
...and give absolutely no consideration
to Spacenoids living in outer space...

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:06.520
...you're naturally going to end up
with a rally or two.

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.390
All they did was appeal
to the government...

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:15.430
...that people must limit their aid
in assisting Earth's ability to recover...

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:21.770
...and they only appealed that all humans
should live in colonies.

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:24.600
But why did Bask end up doing this?

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:26.640
- Why do you think he did this?
- I have no idea.

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:10.350
There's one.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.760
Watch out!

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:27.670
You, in the pilot suit, hands up!

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:31.940
Are you an A.E.U.G.?!

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.410
You're only a kid!

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:37.280
Why are you wearing that pilot suit?

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.750
Why? Well, it's a long story...

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.880
Are you a member of the A.E.U.G.?!

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:44.010
Kamille, where are you?!

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:48.560
If you say one word, I'll kill you.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.320
Are you a member of the Titans?

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:51.860
No, I'm not!

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:54.860
You'll get lost if you wander off too far.

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:58.170
Why that's... Emma Sheen!

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:01.000
- Do you know her?
- Well, yeah.

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:02.440
Could you happen to be...?!

00:16:02.510 --> 00:16:04.530
But I still cannot understand.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:06.270
Why did he overreact like this?

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:08.070
The people of the Earth Federation...

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:14.420
...feared the people who adjusted to their
new living environment in outer space.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.380
Because they were becoming Newtypes?

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.420
Exactly.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:20.050
They think of Newtypes as some kind
of psychics.

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:24.380
So they're afraid these Newtypes
will someday become the ruling class.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:27.500
Can people kill people
for that reason alone?

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:29.670
Sure they can.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:32.130
One could argue
that it's much more reasonable...

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:34.400
...than killing over money.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:35.710
That's a lie!

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:39.040
Why, you're...!

00:16:39.110 --> 00:16:40.240
Lieutenant Lila!

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.470
You're lying!

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:44.850
Bask would never think of killing
so many people for that reason alone!

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.380
Can't you tell by looking around you?

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:49.890
You're being deceived by the logic
of the remnants of the Zabi Clan...

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.680
...who used to do as they wished
with Zeon!

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:56.690
Don't you realize that the Earth Federation
is becoming the next Zabi Clan?

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:58.300
What?!

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:00.430
They're trying to keep the Earth
to themselves.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.800
That person...!

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.530
- It's no use!
- Why?!

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:13.940
She must be here in a mobile suit!

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:16.450
- Let's return to the Argama!
- Right!

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:19.680
My hunch was correct.

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:21.180
She's quite skilled.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.150
Seemingly, the enemy's here on only one
Salamis-class ship!

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.420
<i>Three mobile suits!</i>

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:34.930
Kamille will lead the attack, followed
by the Rick Dias team, which will support him.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.760
<i>Are you testing Kamille?</i>

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:38.730
I'm checking the abilities
of the Gundam Mk. II.

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:48.310
<i>Kamille, get in front of the Argama!</i>

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:50.350
<i>The Rick Dias team will spread to the sides!</i>

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:51.710
Roger!

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.680
<i>I'm borrowing Lieutenant Apolly's</i>
<i>mobile suit.</i>

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.680
Gundam Mk. II, moving out!

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.460
Kamille, let's do it!

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:08.500
<i>Okay!</i>

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:27.120
That's... the person we just met!

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:30.690
I wonder if the pilot
is that smart-mouthed officer?

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:57.240
Are you Lieutenant Lila?!

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.750
That voice... it's the kid I encountered.

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:02.050
Lieutenant Lila!

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:04.420
You heard what Lieutenant Quattro
said back there!

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.390
Stop the insolent talk!

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:10.920
If you're going to fight, I'll shoot!

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:19.430
He's strong! Has he always been piloting
this Gundam Mk. II?!

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:25.910
Detecting light flashes from a battle
close to Colony 30!

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:28.280
So Lieutenant Lila guessed it correctly.

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:31.910
This guy is a Newtype!

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:35.980
But he's a kid! He's just a kid!

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.860
I'm a regular pilot!

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:50.370
There's no way I can lose to that kid!

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:56.200
Lieutenant, you've lost your cool!

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.040
Vanished?!

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:02.980
Lieutenant Commander!

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.710
Why won't you send out reinforcements?!

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:07.750
We shall wait for the Argama
to use up more of their resources.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:12.290
At the same time, this will teach you
to become a better officer, Lieutenant.

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:16.920
A soldier must have the skills
to control his personal emotions.

00:20:57.870 --> 00:20:59.560
I'm not about to lose to that little brat!

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:07.970
It's just as I said to Jamaican!

00:21:08.050 --> 00:21:11.110
Don't take this guy lightly, Jerid!
He isn't just anyone!

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:14.180
<i>I see.</i>

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:17.720
<i>I just admitted that the child isn't just anyone.</i>

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:20.780
<i>And this realization unconsciously</i>
<i>turns into antipathy...!</i>

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:25.090
<i>So that's what it means to be an Oldtype...!</i>

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:33.030
<i>Jerid...!</i>

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:33.970
Lila...?!

00:21:34.170 --> 00:21:35.370
How clumsy of her!

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:41.610
Stop it! This battle is over!

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.520
<i>If you become a fine man...!</i>

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:52.720
Hey! What were you trying
to tell me, Lieutenant?!

00:21:56.690 --> 00:22:00.150
Congratulations!
You are now a full-fledged pilot.

00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:01.360
You're really something.

00:22:01.430 --> 00:22:04.890
It's way better than winning
some mobile suit tournament!

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:08.730
You're the second coming of Amuro Ray!

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:11.570
I agree, Kamille Bidan.

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:13.640
Stop it!

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:16.410
I haven't made the decision
to become a soldier yet.

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:20.080
I'd rather remain as I am now...

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:22.250
...for a little while longer.

00:22:23.190 --> 00:22:27.180
<i>This boy is sensing something that I cannot...</i>

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.350 --> 00:23:47.870
Jerid tries to avenge the death of Lila.

00:23:47.950 --> 00:23:50.250
His Galbaldy enters a desperate battle
against the Gundam Mk. II...

00:23:50.620 --> 00:23:53.550
...within the gravitational field
of the Moon.

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:57.080
Facing Jerid's intense attacks,
Kamille experiences an outburst of emotion.

00:23:57.790 --> 00:24:01.060
In the meantime, the A.E.U.G.
was attempting to proceed...

00:24:01.130 --> 00:24:03.260
...with a large-scale operation
to break the deadlock.

00:24:03.760 --> 00:24:07.570
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"The Dark Side of the Moon".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
The Dark Side of The Moon

00:24:08.440 --> 00:24:10.970
You will see the tears of time.
